[[:db/retract 17592186220547 :answer-field/choices 17592186220548] [:db/retract 17592186220547 :answer-field/choices 17592186220549] [:db/retract 17592186220547 :answer-field/choices 17592186220550] [:db/retract 17592186220547 :answer-field/choices 17592186220551] [:db/retract 17592186220547 :answer-field/choices 17592186220552] [:db/retract 17592186310795 :answer-field/choices 17592186309929] [:db/retract 17592186311288 :answer-field/choices 17592186308837] [:db/retract 17592186310826 :answer-field/choices 17592186308856] [:db/retract 17592186220601 :answer-field/choices 17592186220603] [:db/retract 17592186220601 :answer-field/choices 17592186220606] [:db/retract 17592186220596 :answer-field/choices 17592186220600] [:db/retract 17592186220596 :answer-field/choices 17592186220597] [:db/retract 17592186220596 :answer-field/choices 17592186220598] [:db/retract 17592186220596 :answer-field/choices 17592186220599] {:db/id 17592186221420 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0f204e80-4d56-5e54-8e44-fafc75ad1af8" "question-5c4c6b4c-9f70-5e9c-b320-c7133b929a75" "question-ffe871d4-6b88-566a-ad57-5a37491576bb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221191 :question/problem "![](images/28/28eeada9d539377f372fd73155f08215e6a0eb3b3503b88e05c85e38977c024a.svg)\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions $\\mathbf x_1$ and $\\mathbf x_2,$ shown above. Find the fundamental matrix for the system." :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system $\\mathbf{x}' = A \\mathbf{x},$ where $A$ is an $n \\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $\\Phi(t)$ of the system is an $n \\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our cases, we have a $2 \\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}=[\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}=[\\begin{aligned}4t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 4{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n![](images/89/892921f10f5b3db34b140a6d7608bdb4771fd1ad055319e7ff5d4edceb527d3a.svg)\n\n**Note:** The columns of $\\Phi$ can be written in any order." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-df1d5701-ba5a-54b3-9982-7187c6baef60"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221193 :question/problem "Consider the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2 \\times 2$ matrix. Let $\\Phi(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $\\Phi(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation $\\Phi'(t) = A \\, \\Phi(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $\\big[ \\mathbf{a}, \\: \\mathbf{b} \\big]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}.$*\n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\Phi(t) = \\big[ \\mathbf{x}_1(t), \\: \\mathbf{x}_2(t) \\big]$\n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}_1'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}_1(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}_2'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}_2(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\Phi'(t) = \\big[ \\mathbf{x}_1'(t), \\: \\mathbf{x}_2'(t) \\big]$\n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $\\Phi'(t) =  \\big[ A \\mathbf{x}_1(t), \\: A \\mathbf{x}_2(t) \\big]$\n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\Phi'(t) = A \\big[ \\mathbf{x}_1(t), \\: \\mathbf{x}_2(t) \\big]$\n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\Phi'(t) = A \\Phi(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L2}$ follows from the fact that ![](images/03/036695dd1a6ae9a121d25cae37b1ba7be7e77502b99335391da8d1d8d04972be.svg).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L6}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L5}$ by ![](images/27/27f914bbca34dfde3debdcf58eb5a2205eda059ceafa10bf6964bb7c6a984d1c.svg).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L7}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L6}$ and substitution from line ![](images/b4/b48e9d724fed6566873ba6c844fcfa10c92fcd810012da503960972f8c4105c3.svg)." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221422 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dc97c5df-528b-5640-b7e6-250d27836f61" "question-9ce1dad2-2fca-5e8c-94e6-f02fef65fbf6" "question-a456bad8-fb03-5da0-aae9-4b577c9cb688"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221192 :question/problem "![](images/23/23c904878889e799744f2f4df095727d82a26050d15a01e0df06be6e3838b48d.svg)\nConsider the system of linear ODEs $\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x}$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix $\\Phi(t)$ for this system." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\mathbf x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system $\\mathbf x'(t) = A\\mathbf x(t),$ denoted $\\Phi_0(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t) = A\\Phi_0(t), \\quad \\Phi_0(0)  = I_n,\n$$\n\nwhere $I_n$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & -7{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda) = \\alpha_1 \\lambda + \\alpha_0.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1 = 7\\textrm{i}t, \\qquad\n\\lambda_2 = -7\\textrm{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((7\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(7\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(7\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+7\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{7t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0$ into the expressions for the required entries of $e^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{7t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n![](images/74/744b1de9acba2740bac7ebc54d79fb7ae82e98cb0576492f4d9503bb0b2a71a8.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-0f204e80-4d56-5e54-8e44-fafc75ad1af8" :question/id #uuid "0f204e80-4d56-5e54-8e44-fafc75ad1af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334325" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}=[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-509a43d8-3e68-51c3-84c7-64c7f6910514"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-509a43d8-3e68-51c3-84c7-64c7f6910514" :answer-field/id #uuid "509a43d8-3e68-51c3-84c7-64c7f6910514" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a8abf479-af90-51de-b6dd-86215d035d49" :answer-field/choices ["answer-434d7ea8-e63a-51b4-84d2-ca9a28788176" "answer-2b36e15d-837a-5f85-9a7f-91f066b4c4fd" "answer-bddbb522-2d10-5aec-9ed3-ceed476b3b3f" "answer-a8abf479-af90-51de-b6dd-86215d035d49" "answer-7038d0fd-b4be-5ac4-85f1-ceeccda1e156"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-434d7ea8-e63a-51b4-84d2-ca9a28788176" :answer/id #uuid "434d7ea8-e63a-51b4-84d2-ca9a28788176" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & t \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b36e15d-837a-5f85-9a7f-91f066b4c4fd" :answer/id #uuid "2b36e15d-837a-5f85-9a7f-91f066b4c4fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bddbb522-2d10-5aec-9ed3-ceed476b3b3f" :answer/id #uuid "bddbb522-2d10-5aec-9ed3-ceed476b3b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{4t} & {e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8abf479-af90-51de-b6dd-86215d035d49" :answer/id #uuid "a8abf479-af90-51de-b6dd-86215d035d49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7038d0fd-b4be-5ac4-85f1-ceeccda1e156" :answer/id #uuid "7038d0fd-b4be-5ac4-85f1-ceeccda1e156" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4} & {e}^{4} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5c4c6b4c-9f70-5e9c-b320-c7133b929a75" :question/id #uuid "5c4c6b4c-9f70-5e9c-b320-c7133b929a75" :question/math-academy-id "q-334275" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{3t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental matrix could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & 3{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-97a95112-8d67-5abc-bdfb-cee7755e29a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97a95112-8d67-5abc-bdfb-cee7755e29a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "97a95112-8d67-5abc-bdfb-cee7755e29a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-23e9ec62-9362-5bd5-ab4e-ea2a807a4d0a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15a6f6fa-d163-59c9-8941-abbf24e3752e" "answer-ce05c0b9-0887-59c7-99c8-8f8b04b83fc9" "answer-23e9ec62-9362-5bd5-ab4e-ea2a807a4d0a" "answer-83d316e3-9443-5fad-b4ad-57ed67049c56" "answer-5416c979-f7bd-5995-af0d-eb24dc7ca789"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15a6f6fa-d163-59c9-8941-abbf24e3752e" :answer/id #uuid "15a6f6fa-d163-59c9-8941-abbf24e3752e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce05c0b9-0887-59c7-99c8-8f8b04b83fc9" :answer/id #uuid "ce05c0b9-0887-59c7-99c8-8f8b04b83fc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23e9ec62-9362-5bd5-ab4e-ea2a807a4d0a" :answer/id #uuid "23e9ec62-9362-5bd5-ab4e-ea2a807a4d0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & 3{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83d316e3-9443-5fad-b4ad-57ed67049c56" :answer/id #uuid "83d316e3-9443-5fad-b4ad-57ed67049c56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} & {e}^{2t} \\\\ -{e}^{3t} & 3{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5416c979-f7bd-5995-af0d-eb24dc7ca789" :answer/id #uuid "5416c979-f7bd-5995-af0d-eb24dc7ca789" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2} & -{e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{2} & 3{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221985 :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our cases, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220547 :answer-field/correct "answer-feb3ec21-6632-5781-b732-b19423bbbfa7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0388fd29-b8b2-576b-a6c9-9265590bee1c" "answer-feb3ec21-6632-5781-b732-b19423bbbfa7" "answer-bb791218-a743-55a3-afe5-6608ffd45328" "answer-135f6c78-b365-50be-89db-444d4d16ab70" "answer-3c74cfd1-a038-5c50-bfb1-5cecb7ed1534"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0388fd29-b8b2-576b-a6c9-9265590bee1c" :answer/id #uuid "0388fd29-b8b2-576b-a6c9-9265590bee1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-feb3ec21-6632-5781-b732-b19423bbbfa7" :answer/id #uuid "feb3ec21-6632-5781-b732-b19423bbbfa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb791218-a743-55a3-afe5-6608ffd45328" :answer/id #uuid "bb791218-a743-55a3-afe5-6608ffd45328" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-135f6c78-b365-50be-89db-444d4d16ab70" :answer/id #uuid "135f6c78-b365-50be-89db-444d4d16ab70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-2t} & -{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c74cfd1-a038-5c50-bfb1-5cecb7ed1534" :answer/id #uuid "3c74cfd1-a038-5c50-bfb1-5cecb7ed1534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-2} & -{e}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{-2} & {e}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ffe871d4-6b88-566a-ad57-5a37491576bb" :question/id #uuid "ffe871d4-6b88-566a-ad57-5a37491576bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-334334" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our cases, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e91a5522-798b-57e6-88b5-94ab4c878dba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e91a5522-798b-57e6-88b5-94ab4c878dba" :answer-field/id #uuid "e91a5522-798b-57e6-88b5-94ab4c878dba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-37568771-74a7-5505-977e-6eec3397c6d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4701bacd-a91b-57c5-b9a7-cab331e6593b" "answer-2578d0cc-6b4e-585f-96d2-111f7061558f" "answer-37568771-74a7-5505-977e-6eec3397c6d4" "answer-60edb6b1-d8a3-56fd-94b1-f065189fab74" "answer-f1522afb-a24d-588d-823e-4a33b44528cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4701bacd-a91b-57c5-b9a7-cab331e6593b" :answer/id #uuid "4701bacd-a91b-57c5-b9a7-cab331e6593b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2578d0cc-6b4e-585f-96d2-111f7061558f" :answer/id #uuid "2578d0cc-6b4e-585f-96d2-111f7061558f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37568771-74a7-5505-977e-6eec3397c6d4" :answer/id #uuid "37568771-74a7-5505-977e-6eec3397c6d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60edb6b1-d8a3-56fd-94b1-f065189fab74" :answer/id #uuid "60edb6b1-d8a3-56fd-94b1-f065189fab74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & {e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1522afb-a24d-588d-823e-4a33b44528cf" :answer/id #uuid "f1522afb-a24d-588d-823e-4a33b44528cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡1 & -{e}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡1 \\\\ {e}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡1 & {e}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186310795 :answer-field/correct 17592186308757 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311288 :answer-field/correct 17592186309737 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186310826 :answer-field/correct 17592186309969 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221990 :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line {{field-3}} by the properties of invertible matrices." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Recall that a matrix has linearly independent columns if and only if its determinant is nonzero. Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for any particular $t,$\n\n$$\ndet(Φ(t))\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{the properties of determinants}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Recall that a square matrix is invertible when its determinant is nonzero. Since in $\\text{L3}$ we have that $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t,$ it follows that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t.$ Thus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by the properties of invertible matrices." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220591 :answer-field/correct 17592186220592 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220601 :answer-field/correct 17592186220605 :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee6b0878-88fc-5098-98f5-9eeb896f07d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee6b0878-88fc-5098-98f5-9eeb896f07d6" :answer/id #uuid "ee6b0878-88fc-5098-98f5-9eeb896f07d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}^{′}=A\\,Φ$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220596 :answer-field/correct "answer-1dcb761f-eaed-55a9-ad0a-3da04843c7e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0e243901-1d01-5ec9-9cdc-6cb103946683" "answer-f947d07b-6d00-57b7-a3fe-19a08102e66a" "answer-1dcb761f-eaed-55a9-ad0a-3da04843c7e6" "answer-4832e2c7-75c3-5827-8346-bf8d89ce6137"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e243901-1d01-5ec9-9cdc-6cb103946683" :answer/id #uuid "0e243901-1d01-5ec9-9cdc-6cb103946683" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f947d07b-6d00-57b7-a3fe-19a08102e66a" :answer/id #uuid "f947d07b-6d00-57b7-a3fe-19a08102e66a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dcb761f-eaed-55a9-ad0a-3da04843c7e6" :answer/id #uuid "1dcb761f-eaed-55a9-ad0a-3da04843c7e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4832e2c7-75c3-5827-8346-bf8d89ce6137" :answer/id #uuid "4832e2c7-75c3-5827-8346-bf8d89ce6137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-df1d5701-ba5a-54b3-9982-7187c6baef60" :question/id #uuid "df1d5701-ba5a-54b3-9982-7187c6baef60" :question/math-academy-id "q-336312" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ and substitution from line {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)],$ the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating each column}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its \ncolumns are linearly independent solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ Line $\\text{L1}$ identifies ${x}_{1}(t)$ as a column of $Φ(t),$ so ${x}_{1}(t)$ must satisfy the differential equation. In particular,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ From $\\text{L6}$ we have ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)].$ Using $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$ from $\\text{L1},$ we substitute to obtain ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t).$ Thus, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by substitution from $\\text{L1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8ae518a-9958-5b32-a5fd-7a9d3da57763" "answer-field-2028cfb9-9d36-500c-b53c-d5c401100c51" "answer-field-95dff24a-69a1-5c42-aa00-bca2089747a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8ae518a-9958-5b32-a5fd-7a9d3da57763" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ae518a-9958-5b32-a5fd-7a9d3da57763" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-afe05a9e-d5c2-5aa1-9814-2d2e80429809" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4336788-b670-5b22-9efc-4971c7505f31" "answer-afe05a9e-d5c2-5aa1-9814-2d2e80429809" "answer-14fbbddb-48b0-5865-92fb-6528fd13c65e" "answer-02322a89-1398-5bad-8e30-a0a0a268214d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4336788-b670-5b22-9efc-4971c7505f31" :answer/id #uuid "d4336788-b670-5b22-9efc-4971c7505f31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afe05a9e-d5c2-5aa1-9814-2d2e80429809" :answer/id #uuid "afe05a9e-d5c2-5aa1-9814-2d2e80429809" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14fbbddb-48b0-5865-92fb-6528fd13c65e" :answer/id #uuid "14fbbddb-48b0-5865-92fb-6528fd13c65e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02322a89-1398-5bad-8e30-a0a0a268214d" :answer/id #uuid "02322a89-1398-5bad-8e30-a0a0a268214d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2028cfb9-9d36-500c-b53c-d5c401100c51" :answer-field/id #uuid "2028cfb9-9d36-500c-b53c-d5c401100c51" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e802edfb-19c6-540a-a7d5-687f645229b2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01bc519d-9d8a-5a50-9ddd-0576fdcea192" "answer-4fee71ee-9bfc-53d1-9720-277b632cbc77" "answer-e802edfb-19c6-540a-a7d5-687f645229b2" "answer-99dac2c2-2f9a-5177-aec9-2c19611bdcf2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01bc519d-9d8a-5a50-9ddd-0576fdcea192" :answer/id #uuid "01bc519d-9d8a-5a50-9ddd-0576fdcea192" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ is diagonalizable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fee71ee-9bfc-53d1-9720-277b632cbc77" :answer/id #uuid "4fee71ee-9bfc-53d1-9720-277b632cbc77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e802edfb-19c6-540a-a7d5-687f645229b2" :answer/id #uuid "e802edfb-19c6-540a-a7d5-687f645229b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99dac2c2-2f9a-5177-aec9-2c19611bdcf2" :answer/id #uuid "99dac2c2-2f9a-5177-aec9-2c19611bdcf2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-95dff24a-69a1-5c42-aa00-bca2089747a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "95dff24a-69a1-5c42-aa00-bca2089747a2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-97e4fa85-19f4-5d72-a2e5-d206dea9dd14" :answer-field/choices ["answer-97e4fa85-19f4-5d72-a2e5-d206dea9dd14" "answer-c1306f31-3a02-5b1e-8df0-d8052ca6d7e8" "answer-fed7e9c9-709f-5270-9ace-aa401742d738" "answer-3ad643c3-58b8-599d-80d5-1120b49cec66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97e4fa85-19f4-5d72-a2e5-d206dea9dd14" :answer/id #uuid "97e4fa85-19f4-5d72-a2e5-d206dea9dd14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1306f31-3a02-5b1e-8df0-d8052ca6d7e8" :answer/id #uuid "c1306f31-3a02-5b1e-8df0-d8052ca6d7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fed7e9c9-709f-5270-9ace-aa401742d738" :answer/id #uuid "fed7e9c9-709f-5270-9ace-aa401742d738" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ad643c3-58b8-599d-80d5-1120b49cec66" :answer/id #uuid "3ad643c3-58b8-599d-80d5-1120b49cec66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dc97c5df-528b-5640-b7e6-250d27836f61" :question/id #uuid "dc97c5df-528b-5640-b7e6-250d27836f61" :question/math-academy-id "q-334495" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 0 & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-t)={e}^{-t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(-t)={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-t{e}^{-t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t}(1+t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-{e}^{-t}t+{e}^{-t}(1+t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & ={e}^{-t}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-608539f1-56a3-549b-9b86-eeadf8729d50" "answer-field-335beb98-a9f9-5f49-b0ce-c12df9395ecb" "answer-field-adc78c25-850b-52fa-9f2b-9ea555ee6ffa" "answer-field-c3a781cc-504f-5f42-9f24-00ce26484a8c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-608539f1-56a3-549b-9b86-eeadf8729d50" :answer-field/id #uuid "608539f1-56a3-549b-9b86-eeadf8729d50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-571ee1e9-f789-58d1-979f-dadab4a9282e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-571ee1e9-f789-58d1-979f-dadab4a9282e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-571ee1e9-f789-58d1-979f-dadab4a9282e" :answer/id #uuid "571ee1e9-f789-58d1-979f-dadab4a9282e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-335beb98-a9f9-5f49-b0ce-c12df9395ecb" :answer-field/id #uuid "335beb98-a9f9-5f49-b0ce-c12df9395ecb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-afec3c4b-9a72-5853-9cc0-0f4f9ba6a7ce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-afec3c4b-9a72-5853-9cc0-0f4f9ba6a7ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afec3c4b-9a72-5853-9cc0-0f4f9ba6a7ce" :answer/id #uuid "afec3c4b-9a72-5853-9cc0-0f4f9ba6a7ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "te^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-adc78c25-850b-52fa-9f2b-9ea555ee6ffa" :answer-field/id #uuid "adc78c25-850b-52fa-9f2b-9ea555ee6ffa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f915cb8f-1503-5790-a5be-ea9e1669ff66" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f915cb8f-1503-5790-a5be-ea9e1669ff66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f915cb8f-1503-5790-a5be-ea9e1669ff66" :answer/id #uuid "f915cb8f-1503-5790-a5be-ea9e1669ff66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3a781cc-504f-5f42-9f24-00ce26484a8c" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a781cc-504f-5f42-9f24-00ce26484a8c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5a869c1f-ede5-5da6-a338-863911576984" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a869c1f-ede5-5da6-a338-863911576984"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a869c1f-ede5-5da6-a338-863911576984" :answer/id #uuid "5a869c1f-ede5-5da6-a338-863911576984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ce1dad2-2fca-5e8c-94e6-f02fef65fbf6" :question/id #uuid "9ce1dad2-2fca-5e8c-94e6-f02fef65fbf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334378" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -3{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-3\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((3\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(3\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(3\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+3\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a293f925-01c4-58f6-9d3b-c977e87aacb0" "answer-field-2a55abe9-c911-599b-b2a8-84db01e3afe2" "answer-field-17a3fa21-8b4b-539e-b4a9-7b74df9dfc26" "answer-field-fa9dd6f0-1904-5376-ac44-6fbcd00dad87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a293f925-01c4-58f6-9d3b-c977e87aacb0" :answer-field/id #uuid "a293f925-01c4-58f6-9d3b-c977e87aacb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bde2eae0-1495-58c1-8985-d89c236173c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bde2eae0-1495-58c1-8985-d89c236173c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bde2eae0-1495-58c1-8985-d89c236173c5" :answer/id #uuid "bde2eae0-1495-58c1-8985-d89c236173c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2a55abe9-c911-599b-b2a8-84db01e3afe2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a55abe9-c911-599b-b2a8-84db01e3afe2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-966ff2c0-480f-5877-9989-0745484cb033" :answer-field/choices ["answer-966ff2c0-480f-5877-9989-0745484cb033"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-966ff2c0-480f-5877-9989-0745484cb033" :answer/id #uuid "966ff2c0-480f-5877-9989-0745484cb033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sin(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17a3fa21-8b4b-539e-b4a9-7b74df9dfc26" :answer-field/id #uuid "17a3fa21-8b4b-539e-b4a9-7b74df9dfc26" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-447904f5-55a6-51ca-8b1d-4ad7c937739c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-447904f5-55a6-51ca-8b1d-4ad7c937739c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-447904f5-55a6-51ca-8b1d-4ad7c937739c" :answer/id #uuid "447904f5-55a6-51ca-8b1d-4ad7c937739c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sin(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa9dd6f0-1904-5376-ac44-6fbcd00dad87" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa9dd6f0-1904-5376-ac44-6fbcd00dad87" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0df8888c-7ce2-54cf-89a5-a57b8363008d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0df8888c-7ce2-54cf-89a5-a57b8363008d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0df8888c-7ce2-54cf-89a5-a57b8363008d" :answer/id #uuid "0df8888c-7ce2-54cf-89a5-a57b8363008d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221989 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((2\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(2\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(2\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+2\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186307871 :answer-field/correct "answer-caa9d9cb-c73f-5b34-8a78-86a7733240c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-caa9d9cb-c73f-5b34-8a78-86a7733240c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caa9d9cb-c73f-5b34-8a78-86a7733240c8" :answer/id #uuid "caa9d9cb-c73f-5b34-8a78-86a7733240c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186308289 :answer-field/correct "answer-62e44a13-82dc-5b4c-af8f-b45690546571" :answer-field/choices ["answer-62e44a13-82dc-5b4c-af8f-b45690546571"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62e44a13-82dc-5b4c-af8f-b45690546571" :answer/id #uuid "62e44a13-82dc-5b4c-af8f-b45690546571" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sin(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186307701 :answer-field/correct "answer-18f3666c-fa87-56a3-a25f-71b0d5b23487" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18f3666c-fa87-56a3-a25f-71b0d5b23487"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18f3666c-fa87-56a3-a25f-71b0d5b23487" :answer/id #uuid "18f3666c-fa87-56a3-a25f-71b0d5b23487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sin(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186307700 :answer-field/correct "answer-1727af84-c111-5aa6-af98-970d01d617df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1727af84-c111-5aa6-af98-970d01d617df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1727af84-c111-5aa6-af98-970d01d617df" :answer/id #uuid "1727af84-c111-5aa6-af98-970d01d617df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186365668 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-5t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=5t,\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-5t)={e}^{-5t} \\\\ r(5t)={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-5t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-5t} \\\\ 5t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-10t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{10t}({e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{10t}({e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t} & {e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t} & {e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186365671 :answer-field/correct "answer-90a5ac54-ed2a-5377-933c-378e5c24686e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-90a5ac54-ed2a-5377-933c-378e5c24686e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90a5ac54-ed2a-5377-933c-378e5c24686e" :answer/id #uuid "90a5ac54-ed2a-5377-933c-378e5c24686e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{5t}+e^{-5t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186365669 :answer-field/correct "answer-9e6ed429-cb7b-5097-aa61-71d601e00811" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e6ed429-cb7b-5097-aa61-71d601e00811"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e6ed429-cb7b-5097-aa61-71d601e00811" :answer/id #uuid "9e6ed429-cb7b-5097-aa61-71d601e00811" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{5t}+e^{-5t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a456bad8-fb03-5da0-aae9-4b577c9cb688" :question/id #uuid "a456bad8-fb03-5da0-aae9-4b577c9cb688" :question/math-academy-id "q-334460" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=t\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=3t\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(t)={e}^{t} \\\\ r(3t)={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t} \\\\ 3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtract the first equation from the second one, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{t}}{2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{3{e}^{t}-{e}^{3t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the diagonal entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{t}}{2t}\\cdot t+\\frac{3{e}^{t}-{e}^{3t}}{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{t} \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =3\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{t}}{2t}\\cdot t+\\frac{3{e}^{t}-{e}^{3t}}{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d982dfa-f791-5977-9e71-767b13c5022b" "answer-field-5ac308e4-863c-58ff-b1ad-02a8ca98b2f4" "answer-field-6500511e-9f0a-5ef7-9462-e2cebae0ac35" "answer-field-0b38ef76-8e2e-55bc-a30d-26d2bb7b9989"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d982dfa-f791-5977-9e71-767b13c5022b" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d982dfa-f791-5977-9e71-767b13c5022b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1e574707-9ebd-551d-a80e-32bc19c039cf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e574707-9ebd-551d-a80e-32bc19c039cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e574707-9ebd-551d-a80e-32bc19c039cf" :answer/id #uuid "1e574707-9ebd-551d-a80e-32bc19c039cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5ac308e4-863c-58ff-b1ad-02a8ca98b2f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac308e4-863c-58ff-b1ad-02a8ca98b2f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7a7f68b9-b84b-550d-8d8e-f599f80550fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a7f68b9-b84b-550d-8d8e-f599f80550fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a7f68b9-b84b-550d-8d8e-f599f80550fd" :answer/id #uuid "7a7f68b9-b84b-550d-8d8e-f599f80550fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6500511e-9f0a-5ef7-9462-e2cebae0ac35" :answer-field/id #uuid "6500511e-9f0a-5ef7-9462-e2cebae0ac35" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-11f4854c-8ae9-549a-b2bb-c9073cef5ff2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-11f4854c-8ae9-549a-b2bb-c9073cef5ff2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11f4854c-8ae9-549a-b2bb-c9073cef5ff2" :answer/id #uuid "11f4854c-8ae9-549a-b2bb-c9073cef5ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0b38ef76-8e2e-55bc-a30d-26d2bb7b9989" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b38ef76-8e2e-55bc-a30d-26d2bb7b9989" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-64a42564-d378-5079-b530-a07bf0b2b025" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64a42564-d378-5079-b530-a07bf0b2b025"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64a42564-d378-5079-b530-a07bf0b2b025" :answer/id #uuid "64a42564-d378-5079-b530-a07bf0b2b025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186222503 :tutorial/content "Again, let $\\Phi(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for the linear system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix. The fundamental matrices have the following important properties.\n\n1\\. *Satisfies the underlying system*. Indeed, since each column of $\\Phi(t)$ is a solution of the system, we have\n\n  $$\n  \\Phi'(t) = A\\,\\Phi(t).\n  $$\n\n2\\. *Invertibility*. The columns of $\\Phi(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t,$ so\n\n  $$\n  \\det\\Phi(t)\\neq 0\n  $$\n\n  for all $t.$ In particular, $\\Phi(t)$ is invertible for all $t.$\n\n3\\. *Representation of solutions*. Every solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ of the system can be written in the form\n\n  $$\n  \\mathbf{x}(t)=\\Phi(t)\\,\\mathbf{c},\n  $$\n\n  where $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\n4\\. *Non-uniqueness*. If $C$ is any invertible constant matrix, then\n\n  $$\n  \\Psi(t)=\\Phi(t)\\,C\n  $$\n\n  is also a fundamental matrix for the same system.\n\nWe'll now get some practice." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221468 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
